t more with my  family was important to me as well and  this was an opportunity to kind of  ground myself here in los angeles so why  not  hey natalie this is we every day we we  realize that this is an extraordinary  moment to have an uh two hours of live  television in your case an hour of live  television every day there's a lot going  on in the country of the co-host there  you have the big news background uh how  and will you bring that to the table  when you start today  yeah  well you know i think with my 20 plus  years in journalism and by the way gail  and i go way back to our days in  connecticut together we were competing  morning anchors i'd just like to bring  that up gail  i was going to say we were not at the  same station but i definitely knew who  natalie morales was  definitely knew you  yes i was on the nbc side you were there  cbs side so um you know i do believe  that my role is to help moderate and  guide the discussion especially  involving stories that are perhaps more  topical and newsier stories of the day  and to make sure the facts are out there  and presented but also you know i hope  to have a seriously good time with this  cast  well listen there's no doubt that you  can handle this job you've certainly got  the experience but it is still a big  change for you natalie the day-to-day  but i have no doubt that you will kill  this job but what do you say to other  people who are thinking about making big  changes in their life this is a big one  for you  yeah you know and i've done this before  moving out here to los angeles was  taking a big risk  i do believe though that you know life  is too short life is sweet and we've all  learned that in the last you know couple  of months it's been hard for a lot of  people and i think the opportunities  when they present themselves sometimes  you know  those are the best challenges in life is  when you get a chance to prove yourself  in a different way and that's what i'm  here for i'm game for a